Finally, the `Context Generator` transforms the retrieved `Subgraph` into a format suitable for the LLM. This is handled by `IContextGenerator` and its implementation, `SubgraphToPromptContextGenerator`. The goal is to serialize the graph structure and its relevant properties into a coherent, factual text snippet that the LLM can leverage for reasoning.

```java
// LLMContext.java
public class LLMContext {
    private String promptText;
    private Map<String, Object> metadata; // e.g., source IDs, confidence scores

    // Constructor, getters, setters
}

// IContextGenerator.java
public interface IContextGenerator {
    LLMContext generateContext(ProcessedQuery originalQuery, Subgraph subgraph);
}

// SubgraphToPromptContextGenerator.java
@Service
public class SubgraphToPromptContextGenerator implements IContextGenerator {
    @Override
    public LLMContext generateContext(ProcessedQuery originalQuery, Subgraph subgraph) {
        StringBuilder contextBuilder = new StringBuilder();
        contextBuilder.append("Based on the knowledge graph, here is relevant information to answer the query '").append(originalQuery.getOriginalQuery()).append("':\n\n");

        for (GraphNode node : subgraph.getNodes()) {
            contextBuilder.append("Node: ").append(node.getLabels()).append(" - ").append(node.getProperties().getOrDefault("name", node.getId())).append("\n");
            node.getProperties().forEach((key, value) -> contextBuilder.append("  ").append(key).append(": ").append(value).append("\n"));
        }
        for (GraphRelationship rel : subgraph.getRelationships()) {
            contextBuilder.append("Relationship: (").append(rel.getStartNodeId()).append(") -[").append(rel.getType()).append("]-> (").append(rel.getEndNodeId()).append(")\n");
        }
        return new LLMContext(contextBuilder.toString(), Map.of("nodeCount", subgraph.getNodes().size()));
    }
}
```

These components are orchestrated through a Spring REST controller, providing the external interface for the Graph-Augmented RAG system.

```java
// RagController.java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/rag")
public class RagController {

    private final IQueryProcessor queryProcessor;
    private final IGraphRetrievalEngine graphRetrievalEngine;
    private final IContextGenerator contextGenerator;
    // Assume LLMIntegrationService and ResponseSynthesizer are also injected

    public RagController(IQueryProcessor queryProcessor,
                         IGraphRetrievalEngine graphRetrievalEngine,
                         IContextGenerator contextGenerator) {
        this.queryProcessor = queryProcessor;
        this.graphRetrievalEngine = graphRetrievalEngine;
        this.contextGenerator = contextGenerator;
    }

    @PostMapping("/query")
    public ResponseEntity<String> processRagQuery(@RequestBody String userQuery) {
        // 1. Process Natural Language Query
        ProcessedQuery processedQuery = queryProcessor.process(userQuery);

        // 2. Retrieve Subgraph from Knowledge Graph
        Subgraph subgraph = graphRetrievalEngine.retrieveSubgraph(processedQuery);

        // 3. Generate LLM Context
        LLMContext llmContext = contextGenerator.generateContext(processedQuery, subgraph);

